#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1224
msgid ""
"Assuming you have followed all the recommendations of the Calibration "
"Assistant, the information below can help you identify any remaining "
"problems."
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1229
msgid "Too Few Steps"
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1233
msgid ""
"Calibration was completed with fewer than the desired number of steps.  This "
"is usually caused by changes to binning, focal length, or mount guide speed "
"without using the new-profile-wizard. Run the wizard to restore the correct "
"calibration parameters."
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1243
msgid "Unexpected Rates"
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1246
msgid ""
"Measured RA and Dec movements on the camera sensor aren't related by the "
"expected ratio (cos(dec)).  This can be caused by substantial weight "
"imbalance in Dec or physical resistance to movement because of cables or "
"over-tight gear mesh."
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1261
msgid ""
"The mount is wandering off-target on one axis while PHD2 is measuring "
"movement on the other axis. This can be caused by large periodic error in RA "
"or polar alignment > 10 arc-min. If the orthogonality error is very large, "
"the mount is probably not guiding correctly."
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1271
msgid "Sky Location"
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1275
msgid ""
"Calibration wasn't done with Dec in the range of -20 to +20.  Outside that "
"range, measurement errors may degrade the calibration accuracy. If Dec is "
"outside the range of -60 to +60, declination compensation will not work "
"correctly."
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1285
msgid "Not Enough Movement"
msgstr ""

#: calibration_assistant.cpp:1288
msgid ""
"If you saw an alert saying the guide star did not move enough, the mount may "
"not be receiving or handling guide commands. If you are using an ST-4 guide "
"cable, try replacing it. Otherwise, use the Star-Cross and Manual Guide "
"tools in PHD2 to help isolate the mechanical problem."
msgstr ""

